n" "q-72336" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{4}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13948006/state.json" "file_sha256" "a546006f34867d121c7e5670d5d3de2f8e7d622cd5e0ed87e29b672e0d99d644" "basis" 582 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13948006/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-72336" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\infty "] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13948006/state.json" "file_sha256" "a546006f34867d121c7e5670d5d3de2f8e7d622cd5e0ed87e29b672e0d99d644" "basis" 582 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13948006/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-300" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate $\\displaystyle \\lim_{x\\rightarrow 3}\\dfrac{x^3-27}{x-3}$." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13948006/example-300.json" "file_sha256" "3fa49fb89cc3f449d566bcc77f2daf2d593590a363e8b05788c7b2490422c630" "basis" 582 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13948006/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-336951" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following limit:\n\n${lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+9x-4}{3x+1}=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13953349/state.json" "file_sha256" "6ad16e0bf31b984540cc56371400cb15d1c3833fd3fca01b40283845da06fa50" "basis" 611 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13953349/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-336951" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "In this case, we have an indeterminate form of type $\\frac{\\infty }{\\infty },$ so applying L'Hopital's rule yields\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+9x-4}{3x+1} & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{[2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+9x-4]^{′}}{[3x+1]^{′}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{(\\frac{2}{x}+9)}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{0+9}{3} \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13953349/state.json" "file_sha256" "6ad16e0bf31b984540cc56371400cb15d1c3833fd3fca01b40283845da06fa50" "basis" 611 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13953349/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-336951" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13953349/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a814142e70c437c40ba89215da0ba258eeafa49bf036e1346036f3d873799939" "basis" 611 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13953349/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-336951" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13953349/state.json" "file_sha256" "6ad16e0bf31b984540cc56371400cb15d1c3833fd3fca01b40283845da06fa50" "basis" 611 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13953349/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-336951" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "3"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13953349/state.json" "file_sha256" "6ad16e0bf31b984540cc56371400cb15d1c3833fd3fca01b40283845da06fa50" "basis" 611 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13953349/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-72335" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "${lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{{e}^{2/{x}^{2}}}{(\\frac{1}{2{x}^{2}})}=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972402/state.json" "file_sha256" "bef90c10f3fe2496b1b1e7b74213c83c0789cb68a20aa5b4aef87a1bb7dab9b6" "basis" 669 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972402/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-72335" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Here the limits of the numerator and denominator are ${lim}_{x\\to 0}{e}^{2/{x}^{2}}=\\infty $ and ${lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{1}{2{x}^{2}}=\\infty ,$ respectively, so we have the case $\\frac{\\infty }{\\infty }.$\n\nApplying L'Hopital's rule, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{{e}^{2/{x}^{2}}}{(\\frac{1}{2{x}^{2}})} & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{{[{e}^{2/{x}^{2}}]}^{′}}{{[\\frac{1}{2{x}^{2}}]}^{′}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{{e}^{2/{x}^{2}}(-\\frac{4}{{x}^{3}})}{(-\\frac{1}{{x}^{3}})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{4{e}^{2/{x}^{2}}\\cancel{(-\\frac{1}{{x}^{3}})}}{\\cancel{(-\\frac{1}{{x}^{3}})}} \\\\  & =4{lim}_{x\\to 0}{e}^{2/{x}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\infty .\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972402/state.json" "file_sha256" "bef90c10f3fe2496b1b1e7b74213c83c0789cb68a20aa5b4aef87a1bb7dab9b6" "basis" 669 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972402/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-72335" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacadem