son"} {"question" "q-114249" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If we plug in $x=-1$ we get the indeterminate form $\\frac{0}{0},$ so  we apply L'Hopital's rule to find the limit:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to -1}\\frac{(x+2)\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+2)-x-1}{{x}^{2}+2x+1} & ={lim}_{x\\to -1}\\frac{{[(x+2)\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+2)-x-1]}^{′}}{{[{x}^{2}+2x+1]}^{′}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to -1}\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+2)}{2x+2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis time, the resulting limit still gives the indeterminate form $\\frac{0}{0}.$ To find the limit, we apply L'Hopital's rule once again. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to -1}\\frac{(x+2)\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+2)-x-1}{{x}^{2}+2x+1} & ={lim}_{x\\to -1}\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+2)}{2x+2} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to -1}\\frac{{[\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+2)]}^{′}}{{[2x+2]}^{′}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to -1}\\frac{(\\frac{1}{x+2})}{2} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to -1}\\frac{1}{2(x+2)} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003623/state.json" "file_sha256" "a27908fcf7e3ee75ae6093cbf46463237bda3d3a1e4f9a015437115aba1b7499" "basis" 1090 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003623/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-114249" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003623/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "285dfc88d1b41ab74575d2f461b238022ea779501eee859121d3b18f9acb4002" "basis" 1090 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003623/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-114249" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/referen