\frac{5}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036388/state.json" "file_sha256" "bc8640589c7211df684243b2fb074e5afc2db0fa731e358093128044afcf5d22" "basis" 1260 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036388/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-31253" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036388/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "3b2a77a80d73e1184b4b9ea714112cff4f9671a324fc00a8a1c05c5def17292b" "basis" 1260 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036388/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-31253" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036388/state.json" "file_sha256" "bc8640589c7211df684243b2fb074e5afc2db0fa731e358093128044afcf5d22" "basis" 1260 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036388/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-31253" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "1"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036388/state.json" "file_sha256" "bc8640589c7211df684243b2fb074e5afc2db0fa731e358093128044afcf5d22" "basis" 1260 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036388/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-31253" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "2"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036388/state.json" "file_sha256" "bc8640589c7211df684243b2fb074e5afc2db0fa731e358093128044afcf5d22" "basis" 1260 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036388/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-31253" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{4}{5}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036388/state.json" "file_sha256" "bc8640589c7211df684243b2fb074e5afc2db0fa731e358093128044afcf5d22" "basis" 1260 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036388/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-31253" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{5}{4}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036388/state.json" "file_sha256" "bc8640589c7211df684243b2fb074e5afc2db0fa731e358093128044afcf5d22" "basis" 1260 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036388/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-31253" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\infty "] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036388/state.json" "file_sha256" "bc8640589c7211df684243b2fb074e5afc2db0fa731e358093128044afcf5d22" "basis" 1260 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036388/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-31253" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{5}{4}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036388/state.json" "file_sha256" "bc8640589c7211df684243b2fb074e5afc2db0fa731e358093128044afcf5d22" "basis" 1260 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036388/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-336971" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following limit:\n\n${lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{{x}^{3}}{{ln}^{2}⁡x}=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036388/state.json" "file_sha256" "bc8640589c7211df684243b2fb074e5afc2db0fa731e358093128044afcf5d22" "basis" 1260 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036388/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-336971" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "In this case, we have an indeterminate form of type $\\frac{\\infty }{\\infty },$ so applying L'Hopital's rule yields\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{{x}^{3}}{{ln}^{2}⁡x} & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{[{x}^{3}]^{′}}{[{ln}^{2}⁡x]^{′}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{3{x}^{2}}{(\\frac{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{x})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{3{x}^{3}}{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis time, the resulting limit still gives the indeterminate form $\\frac{\\infty }{\\infty }.$ To find the limit, we apply L'Hopital's rule once again. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{{x}^{3}}{{ln}^{2}⁡x} & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{[3{x}^{3}]^{′}}{{[2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x]}^{′}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{9{x}^{2}}{(\\frac{2}{x})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{9{x}^{3}}{2} \\\\  & =\\infty .\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036388/state.json" "file_sha256" "bc8640589c7211df684243b2fb074e5afc2db0fa731e358093128044afcf5d22" "basis" 1260 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036388/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-336971" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036388/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "3b2a77a80d73e1184b4b9ea714112cff4f9671a324fc00a8a1c05c5def17292b" "basis" 1260 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036388/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-336971" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036388/state.json" "file_sha256" "bc8640589c7211df684243b2fb074e5afc2db0fa731e358093128044afcf5d22" "basis" 1260 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036388/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-300" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate $\\displaystyle \\lim_{x\\rightarrow 3}\\dfrac{x^3-27}{x-3}$." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036388/example-300.json" "file_sha256" "3fa49fb89cc3f449d566bcc77f2daf2d593590a363e8b05788c7b2490422c630" "basis" 1260 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036388/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-300" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Note that plugging in $x=3$ gives the indeterminate form $\\dfrac{0}{0}.$ However, we can use L'Hopital's rule to find this limit:\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\\lim_{x\\to 3}  \\dfrac {x^3-27}{x-3} \n&= \\lim_{x\\to3}  \\dfrac {[x^3-27]'}{[x-3]'}\\[5pt]\n&= \\lim_{x\\to 3}  \\dfrac {3x^2}{1}\\[5pt]\n&=  3(3)^2\\[5pt]\n&= 27\n}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036388/example-300.json" "file_sha256" "3fa49fb89cc3f449d566bcc77f2daf2d593590a363e8b05788c7b2490422c630" "basis" 1260 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036388/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-301" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate  $\\displaystyle \\lim_{x\\to 0} \\, \\frac {\\sin^2 (2x)}{x^2}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036388/example-301.json" "file_sha256" "0240bd5760ae0f49edcc6a7c9fc2e6f9761a534c0714533e0c12d51dd544327a" "basis" 1260 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036388/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-301" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If we plug in $x=0$ we get the indeterminate form $\\dfrac{0}{0},$ so  we apply L'Hopital's rule to find the limit:\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\\lim_{x\\to0}  \\dfrac{\\sin^2 (2x)}{x^2} &= \\lim_{x\\to 0}  \\dfrac {\\left[\\sin^2 (2x)\\right]'}{[x^2]'}\\[5pt]\n&= \\lim_{x\\to 0}  \\dfrac{2\\cdot \\sin (2x) \\cdot\\cos (2x)\\cdot 2}{2x}\\[5pt]\n&= \\lim_{x\\to 0}{2\\cos (2x)} \\cdot \\lim_{x\\to 0} \\dfrac{\\sin (2x)}{x}\\[5pt]\n&= 2\\cos(2\\cdot 0)\\lim_{x\\to 0}\\dfrac{\\sin (2x)}{x}\\[5pt]\n&= 2\\lim_{x\\to 0}\\dfrac{\\sin (2x)}{x}\n}\n$$\n\nThis time, the resulting limit still gives the indeterminate form $\\dfrac{0}{0}.$ But that's okay, because we can just apply L'Hopital's rule again! We get\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\\lim_{x\\to0}  \\dfrac{\\sin^2 (2x)}{x^2} &= 2\\lim_{x\\to 0}\\dfrac{\\sin (2x)}{x}\\[5pt]\n&=  2\\lim_{x\\to0}  \\dfrac {[\\sin (2x)]'}{[x]'}\\[5pt]\n&=  2\\lim_{x\\to0}  \\dfrac {2\\cos (2x)}{1}\\[5pt]\n&= 4\\cos(2\\cdot 0)\\\n&=4.\n}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036388/example-301.json" "file_sha256" "0240bd5760ae0f49edcc6a7c9fc2e6f9761a534c0714533e0c12d51dd544327a" "basis" 1260 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036388/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-302" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate $\\displaystyle \\lim_{x\\to 0}  \\dfrac{\\ln\\left(x^2\\right)}{\\left(\\dfrac{2}{x^2}\\right)} .$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036388/example-302.json" "file_sha256" "148ec8403f65ecfb7ab128467ee7c615a0853467a05774c8db925ea02236c95a" "basis" 1260 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036388/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-302" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Here the limits of the numerator and denominator are\n$\\displaystyle\n \\lim_{x\\to 0}  \\ln\\left(x^2\\right) = -\\infty$ and $\\displaystyle \\lim_{x\\to 0} \\dfrac{2}{x^2} = \\infty$ respectively,\nso we have the case $\\dfrac{-\\infty}{\\infty}$.\n\nApplying L'Hopital's rule, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\\lim_{x\\to 0}  \\dfrac{\\ln\\left(x^2\\right)}{\\left(\\dfrac{2}{x^2}\\right)} &= \\lim_{x\\to 0}  \\dfrac{[\\ln\\left(x^2\\right)]'}{\\left(\\dfrac{2}{x^2}\\right)'}\\[5pt]\n&= \\lim_{x\\to 0}  \\dfrac{\\left(1/x^2\\right)\\cdot 2x}{-\\left({4}/{x^3}\\right)}\\[5pt]\n&= \\lim_{x\\to 0}  \\dfrac{x^{-2} \\cdot 2x}{-4x^{-3} }\\[5pt]\n&= \\lim_{x\\to 0}  \\dfrac{2x^{-1}}{-4x^{-3} }\\[5pt]\n&= -\\dfrac{1}{2}  \\lim_{x\\to 0} {x^2}\\[5pt]\n&= -\\dfrac{1}{2}\\cdot 0\\[5pt]\n&= 0.\n}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036388/example-302.json" "file_sha256" "148ec8403f65ecfb7ab128467ee7c615a0853467a05774c8db925ea02236c95a" "basis" 1260 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036388/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-303" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate ${\\displaystyle \\lim_{x\\to\\infty}  \\frac {x^6}{5x^6-4} }.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036388/example-303.json" "file_sha256" "3aa3190786d7e95470add384d807b1fabcd71ffff71d43f753bb85d7e5864aee" "basis" 1260 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036388/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-303" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "In this case, we have an indeterminate form of type $\\dfrac{\\infty}{\\infty},$ so applying  L'Hopital's rule yields\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\\lim_{x\\to \\infty}  \\dfrac {x^6}{5x^6-4} &= \\lim_{x\\to\\infty}  \\dfrac {[x^6]'}{[5x^6-4]'}\\\n&= \\lim_{x\\to \\infty}  \\dfrac {6x^5}{5(6x^5)-0}\\\n&=  \\lim_{x\\to \\infty}  \\dfrac {1}{5}\\\n&= \\dfrac{1}{5}.\n}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036388/example-303.json" "file_sha256" "3aa3190786d7e95470add384d807b1fabcd71ffff71d43f753bb85d7e5864aee" "basis" 1260 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14036388/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-336903" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following limit:\n\n$\\,{lim}_{x\\to -4}\\frac{(x+4)^{3}}{3\\sqrt[3]{x+5}-x-7}=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14052886/state.json" "file_sha256" "849e64347e0da4239e484675c4106fd9111c938128c7d13961a0e4bee2930bc0" "basis" 1771 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14052886/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-336903" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If we plug in $x=-4$ we get the indeterminate form $\\frac{0}{0},$ so we apply L'Hopital's rule to find the limit:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to -4}\\frac{(x+4)^{3}}{3\\sqrt[3]{x+5}-x-7} & ={lim}_{x\\to -4}\\frac{{[(x+4)^{3}]}^{′}}{{[3(x+5)^{1/3}-x-7]}^{′}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to -4}\\frac{3(x+4)^{2}}{(x+5)^{-2/3}-1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis time, the resulting limit still gives the indeterminate form $\\frac{0}{0}.$ To find the limit, we apply L'Hopital's rule once again. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to -4}\\frac{3(x+4)^{2}}{(x+5)^{-2/3}-1} & ={lim}_{x\\to -4}\\frac{{[3(x+4)^{2}]}^{′}}{{[(x+5)^{-2/3}-1]}^{′}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to -4}\\frac{6(x+4)}{-\\frac{2}{3}(x+5)^{-5/3}} \\\\  & =-9{lim}_{x\\to -4}(x+4)(x+5)^{5/3} \\\\  & =-9(-4+4)\\,(-4+5)^{5/3} \\\\  & =-9\\cdot 0\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14052886/state.json" "file_sha256" "849e64347e0da4239e484675c4106fd9111c938128c7d13961a0e4bee2930bc0" "basis" 1771 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14052886/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-336903" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14052886/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "78dbd5e2a5fc03c6a49f5b6a945968accd3ed19fd2f255cd3ff5ae43841a69c6" "basis" 1771 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14052886/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-336903" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14052886/state.json" "file_sha256" "849e64347e0da4239e484675c4106fd9111c938128c7d13961a0e4bee2930bc0" "basis" 1771 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14052886/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-31272" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "${lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{4\\sqrt{x+4}-x-8}{{x}^{2}}=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068434/state.json" "file_sha256" "f510fe2b8860606b92c61bb3c98e154cd4cb66bce666d1111228e4b5671d72e5" "basis" 2314 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068434/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-31272" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If we plug in $x=0$ we get the indeterminate form $\\frac{0}{0},$ so  we apply L'Hopital's rule to find the limit:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{4\\sqrt{x+4}-x-8}{{x}^{2}} & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{{[4\\sqrt{x+4}-x-8]}^{′}}{[{x}^{2}]^{′}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{[\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{x+4}}-1]}{2x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis time, the resulting limit still gives the indeterminate form $\\frac{0}{0}.$ To find the limit, we apply L'Hopital's rule once again. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{4\\sqrt{x+4}-x-8}{{x}^{2}} & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{[\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{x+4}}-1]}{2x} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{{[\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{x+4}}-1]}^{′}}{[2x]^{′}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{[-\\frac{1}{(x+4)\\sqrt{x+4}}]}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{[-\\frac{1}{(0+4)\\sqrt{0+4}}]}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{[-\\frac{1}{4(2)}]}{2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{16}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068434/state.json" "file_sha256" "f510fe2b8860606b92c61bb3c98e154cd4cb66bce666d1111228e4b5671d72e5" "basis" 2314 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068434/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-31272" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068434/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "543a47ee29201caea3d4fe4078ab9f2433b6e634fd1408c35864fe779760c0f4" "basis" 2314 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068434/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-31272" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068434/state.json" "file_sha256" "f510fe2b8860606b92c61bb3c98e154cd4cb66bce666d1111228e4b5671d72e5" "basis" 2314 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068434/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-31272" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "-1"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/re